  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 as RNA encoder dramatically outperforms scgpt (~0.72 vs ~0.53), and transformer+weighted is the best aggregation/fusion combo (0.725). However, all 5 experiments used imagenet_vit_l; the image encoder dimension is completely untested. Question: Does swapping to resnet50 with the proven scvi_n200+transformer+weighted stack improve or degrade performance? This is the largest untested design axis. Rationale: With only 4 experiments left, testing the image encoder is the highest-information experiment—if resnet50 is competitive, it opens a new direction; if it underperforms, it confirms imagenet_vit_l is critical and we can focus remaining budget on fine-tuning aggregation/fusion or profile settings. config_024 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) isolates the image encoder change while holding all other parameters at their known-best values."
}

